certificates and the windows of the two spinodal roots of `q`.

Reduced volume `x = v/b`, `θ = R T b / a`, reduced pressure `π = p b² / a`. The isotherm is
`(a/b²) · g θ x` with `g θ x = θ/(x−1) − 1/(x² + x)`; `ψ θ π x = θ log(x−1) + (log(x+1) − log x) − π x`
is a primitive of `g θ − π` on `x > 1`; `g θ' x = q θ x / ((x−1)²(x²+x)²)` with
`q θ x = (2x+1)(x−1)² − θ(x²+x)²`. For every `θ` in a rational interval of width about 10⁻⁹ (endpoints
in `reduced_window`) every Maxwell coexistence state has its reduced pressure in a narrow rational
window (`reduced_window`). Certificates: `runs/2026-11-06T0028Z/scripts/gen_srk.py` (exact rationals).
The last section turns the window into `p_s/P_c` and the acentric factor for Soave's
`a(0.7 T_c) = a_c (1 + κ(1)(1 − √0.7))²`, `κ(1) = 0.480 + 1.574 − 0.176`.
